WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Marcus signs a life application and pays the requested initial premium.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.620
The producer gives him the insurer's receipt and explains its terms.

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.040
That receipt may provide conditional protection, a defined temporary

4
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.520
agreement or only the stated acknowledgment.

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.100
It is not a blank promise that every death will be

6
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:30.420
covered immediately. Identify the amount paid, the required

7
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.700
signatures, eligibility conditions, benefit limits

8
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.520
and termination events. A producer must stay within the insurer's

9
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.560
actual authority. Never replace a written condition with

10
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.020
a reassuring statement that the applicant is definitely covered.

11
00:00:51.714 --> 00:00:56.394
Consider a teaching receipt that requires the applicant to be insurable

12
00:00:56.394 --> 00:01:00.754
exactly as applied for on the later of the application date

13
00:01:00.754 --> 00:01:03.494
and the required examination date.

14
00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:08.194
All other stated conditions are assumed satisfied.

15
00:01:09.154 --> 00:01:14.654
Marcus applies and pays on June third, completes the examination on

16
00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:19.034
June seventh and receives approval on June twelfth.

17
00:01:19.574 --> 00:01:24.294
Under this example, the conditional starting date is June seventh.

18
00:01:24.894 --> 00:01:29.474
The later approval confirms that the stated insurability condition was met.

19
00:01:30.614 --> 00:01:34.974
Do not move every conditional receipt to the application date or

20
00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:38.054
approval date. Read the particular receipt.

21
00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:43.864
Now a different teaching receipt expressly requires home-office approval

22
00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:46.284
before any protection starts.

23
00:01:47.504 --> 00:01:51.964
The application and payment dates stay the same, but approval occurs

24
00:01:51.964 --> 00:01:57.024
on June twelfth. Apply that approval condition instead

25
00:01:57.024 --> 00:02:00.424
of borrowing the June seventh answer from the prior example.

26
00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:05.464
A separate temporary insurance agreement can have its own eligibility,

27
00:02:05.944 --> 00:02:07.584
amount and end date.

28
00:02:08.624 --> 00:02:11.704
None of these labels removes the need to read the terms.

29
00:02:12.504 --> 00:02:16.024
If an applicant dies while underwriting is pending, send the facts

30
00:02:16.024 --> 00:02:17.444
for a proper claim review.

31
00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:22.704
Pending underwriting does not by itself prove either coverage or no

32
00:02:22.704 --> 00:02:27.978
coverage. Elena submits an application without paying

33
00:02:27.978 --> 00:02:31.678
the initial premium and has no temporary insurance agreement.

34
00:02:32.498 --> 00:02:37.058
The insurer sends a policy for delivery subject to payment and

35
00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:40.018
the required confirmation of unchanged health.

36
00:02:41.178 --> 00:02:44.838
Mailing that policy to the producer does not prove these conditions

37
00:02:44.838 --> 00:02:49.758
are complete. Collect the required premium, obtain the truthful delivery

38
00:02:49.758 --> 00:02:52.938
documentation and follow the insurer's instructions.

39
00:02:54.238 --> 00:02:59.158
In a different case, unconditional release of an accepted policy for

40
00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:02.418
delivery may constitute constructive delivery.

41
00:03:03.138 --> 00:03:07.098
Distinguish unconditional release from a file with outstanding conditions.

42
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:12.238
The physical handoff and the legal effective date are not always

43
00:03:12.238 --> 00:03:17.144
the same event. Before the conditional delivery is completed, Elena reports

44
00:03:17.144 --> 00:03:22.384
a new hospitalization. Do not have her sign an unchanged-health

45
00:03:22.384 --> 00:03:24.044
statement that is false.

46
00:03:24.964 --> 00:03:29.304
Follow the insurer's instructions and submit the new facts for review.

47
00:03:30.264 --> 00:03:35.504
If the insurer offers a different amount, premium or classification, explain

48
00:03:35.504 --> 00:03:38.104
the change and obtain the required acceptance.

49
00:03:38.104 --> 00:03:42.444
The applicant does not have to accept a modified offer simply

50
00:03:42.444 --> 00:03:44.504
because an application was signed.

51
00:03:45.264 --> 00:03:49.804
Likewise, a new fact does not authorize an agent to erase

52
00:03:49.804 --> 00:03:53.924
coverage that already became effective under a valid agreement.

53
00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:58.444
Resolve the status from the contract and the actual timeline.

54
00:03:59.346 --> 00:04:04.146
At delivery, review the insured, owner, beneficiary, coverage amount,

55
00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:08.906
riders, premium schedule, guarantees and important limitations.

56
00:04:09.966 --> 00:04:13.426
Explain the applicable return right and how to contact the insurer.

57
00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:18.126
Check that the delivered policy matches the accepted offer and record

58
00:04:18.126 --> 00:04:20.166
the delivery through the approved process.

59
00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:23.786
A policy date may be used to measure anniversaries or insurance

60
00:04:23.786 --> 00:04:27.866
age; that printed date alone does not answer every coverage question.

61
00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:33.066
Keep the application date, receipt date, effective date and delivery date

62
00:04:33.066 --> 00:04:37.586
distinct. The client should leave knowing what is in force, what

63
00:04:37.586 --> 00:04:40.246
must be paid and which rights have a deadline.
